Hello,

To make it easier to develop external, graphical clients,
I've added an option for the nethack.alt.org NetHack to
output extra data in the stream.
To use it, set "vt_tiledata" in the options.

When the option is on, NetHack will output escape codes in
the form "ESC [ ... z", which (should) be ignored by most normal 
terminals.  So, this is not useful in any way for playing
in a normal text terminal.


Currently used codes:

   * "ESC [ 0 ; n z": Start a glyph (aka a tile) number n.
   * "ESC [ 1 z": End a glyph.
   * "ESC [ 2 ; n z": Select a window n to output to. 


Whenever NetHack outputs anything, it will first output
the select window code.

Whenever NetHack outputs a tile, it will first output
the start glyph code, then the escape codes for color
and the glyph character itself, and then the end glyph code.


Basically, this is an expanded version of the "telnettiles"
patch by Justin Hiltscher.

